  "body": "What happens: the MCP tool `convert_tools_to_components` (#4339) is live and is in `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and the site guide. The `camcraft-mcp` skill (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`) has no row for it.\n\nExpected: the skill's tool section has one row for the tool, next to `get_tool_assembly` and `set_tool_assembly`. The row gives the arguments `tools?` (array of tool names) and `dry_run?` (boolean), the preview rows (`tool`, `result` same / different / no match, `differences`, `reason`, `components`, `links`), and the default: without `tools`, only the \"same\" rows convert.\n\nWhy separate: the skill is a process file. A change to it needs `Process change: yes` and a PROCESS_VERSION bump by the merging session. The #4339 PR keeps to product code.\n\nDone means: the skill names the tool with its arguments and its default, the PR body has `Process change: yes`, and `mcp_doc_drift` stays green.\n",
